column78:
This document helped me out a bit: <a href="http://developer.apple.com/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/MemoryMgmt/MemoryMgmt.html" rel="nofollow">http://developer.apple.com/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/Me...</a><p>Also, this has a few rules you can follow: <a href="http://www.stepwise.com/Articles/Technical/2001-03-11.01.html" rel="nofollow">http://www.stepwise.com/Articles/Technical/2001-03-11.01.htm...</a><p>Just remember that adding elements to containers bumps their retain counts. So the following is a common pattern for me:<p><pre><code>  MyClass *c = [[MyClass alloc] init];
  [arr addObject:c];
  [c release];

</code></pre>
If you're returning an object from a method, you probably want to autorelease it.
